				<h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight">Methodology</h1>
				<p class="mt-3 text-base text-foreground-muted">How we evaluate and score AI translation quality.</p>

				<div class="prose prose-base mt-10 text-foreground-muted">
					<h2>Overview</h2>
					<p>M-GATE uses a combination of automatic metrics and human evaluation to produce a holistic picture of translation quality. All models are evaluated under the same conditions on the same test sets.</p>

					<h2>Automatic metrics</h2>
					<p>We report three primary automatic metrics:</p>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>COMET</strong> – a neural reference-based metric trained on human judgements. Scores typically range from 0–100.</li>
						<li><strong>BLEU</strong> – a classic n-gram precision metric. Useful for trend analysis but less correlated with human judgement than COMET.</li>
						<li><strong>ChrF</strong> – character-level F-score, particularly useful for morphologically rich languages.</li>
					</ul>

					<h2>Human evaluation</h2>
					<p>A subset of outputs are evaluated by professional translators using a Direct Assessment (DA) protocol. Evaluators rate fluency and adequacy independently on a 1–5 scale.</p>

					<h2>Test sets</h2>
					<p>We use publicly available test sets from WMT and Flores-200, supplemented with domain-specific sets covering legal, medical, technical, and marketing content.</p>

					<h2>Model evaluation conditions</h2>
					<p>All models are evaluated using default API settings with no system prompt unless required for operation. Temperature is set to 0 for deterministic outputs.</p>

					<h2>Updates</h2>
					<p>The benchmark is updated quarterly. Results from previous quarters are archived and remain accessible.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

